## How the Look Changes Across Seasons Without Ever Losing Its Identity

This is the manicure that does not need to be retired when the weather changes. The palette shifts  cooler and sheerer in summer, deeper and richer in winter  but the aesthetic logic stays identical: shape, finish, cuticle prep. Those three pillars hold across every season.

**Summer.** The palette moves toward its lightest expression. Soap nails, sheer whites, vanilla gloss, milky pink with a pearl chrome veil. The finish gets a slightly higher gloss  sunlight rewards that level of shine. Buttercream becomes the dominant neutral because it reads warm against sun-touched skin. The shape stays almond, possibly slightly shorter. The overall effect is cooler, airier, almost translucent.

