**Bubble nails.** The 2026 evolution of chrome: iridescent chrome powder applied over a neutral base in a translucent, bubble-like finish. Neither mirror nor matte  somewhere between gloss and chrome with a slight holographic depth. It reads luxurious in a way that requires no explanation.

**Soap nails.** The most understated option in the design range. Transparent, sheer, wet-looking. The design *is* the finish  no art, no technique beyond the application. The luxury is entirely in the nail bed quality and the gloss level. Soap nails on an unprepared cuticle look like nothing. Soap nails on a Russian-prepped nail bed with a BIAB base look like everything.

**Tone-on-tone.** A milky base with a slightly deeper milky shade at the tip  the same colour family, different opacity. It is the most invisible-to-anyone-who-isn't-looking nail art within this aesthetic, and the most sophisticated to those who are.

