## The Most Considered Manicure You Can Book

The cashmere coat analogy holds. <strong>Quiet luxury nails</strong> are not the manicure that competes for attention in the room  they are the one that gets noticed anyway, by the people who know what they are looking at.

The nails that look expensive without being loud are not the result of a more timid decision. They are the result of three very specific, very deliberate ones: the almond shape that elongates, the milky or glazed finish that has depth, and the cuticle prep that makes every other choice land. Nail it  all three  and the shade is almost irrelevant. It will look expensive because the decision behind it was.

That is the quiet luxury philosophy, applied. Not restraint for its own sake. Restraint as the boldest possible statement.

